==English==
{{was wotd|2021|April|2}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*per-|*h₂el- (grow)}}
From {{der|en|fr|prolétariat|t=proletariats as a class; state of being a proletariat}}, from {{der|en|la|prōlētārius|t=belonging to the lowest class of citizens, whose only contribution to the state was their offspring; member of this class}} + {{der|en|fr|-at|pos={{glossary|suffix}} denoting actions or the results of actions}}.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=152329|date=December 2020|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=n}}</ref> {{m|la||Prōlētārius}} is derived from {{m|la|prōlēs|t=offspring, posterity}} + {{m|la|-ārius|pos=suffix forming {{glossary|adjective}}s from {{glossary|noun}}s, or forming nouns denoting agents of use from other nouns}}; {{m|la||prōlēs}} is from {{m|la|pro-|pos={{glossary|prefix}} meaning ‘bringing forth or into being; bringing into the open’}} + {{m|la|*olēs}} (a variant of {{m|la|*oleō|t=to grow}}, ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*h₂el-|t=to grow, nourish}}).

